The fork is served by `medium`, which nothing declares.

The same rule as a request naming an undeclared substrate, on the row that
makes the point of declaring them: a fork is how a run reaches a SECOND
substrate -- an interview on a small local model beside a main lane on a large
one -- so a fork is the row most likely to name one the regime forgot.

Fixtured because the review found the fork arm of this check unexercised:
deleting it from the match left every test green.
